# Shell scripts MUST be LF. Always.
#
# deploy/pod_setup.sh was committed from Windows and sat in the tree with CRLF
# endings. That is not untidiness: bash on Linux treats the CR as part of each
# token, so the script dies on its first line with `$'\r': command not found`.
# These scripts are piped straight into a billing GPU pod over ssh, so a CRLF
# checkout does not fail cheaply -- it fails after the pod is already running.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for everything else a Linux host executes verbatim.
*.service text eol=lf
*.timer   text eol=lf
Caddyfile text eol=lf
